.git
.github
.idea
vendor
node_modules
storage/logs/*
storage/framework/cache/*
storage/framework/sessions/*
storage/framework/views/*
# Fake-disk scratch written by in-container test runs, owned by root. Never
# belongs in the image, and its presence breaks the build on a permission error.
storage/framework/testing/*
# Generated workbooks are runtime data written by the container as root; they must
# never be baked into the image, and leaving them here breaks the build on a
# permission error.
storage/app/reports/*
loadtest/results/*
# The developer's .env must never be baked into the image: it ships a real APP_KEY
# and database credentials in a layer, and — worse — it defeats the production
# config guard in docker/entrypoint.sh, which refuses to boot when no .env is
# mounted. A baked .env means that guard finds a file, sees APP_ENV=local, and
# starts on the developer's configuration instead of failing. .env.example is
# still copied in and is what a local container boots from.
.env
!.env.example
openspec
*.md
!README.md
task.pdf
